Subject: [PATCH] ao_audiotrack: wait for the core's audio instead of writing nothing

When the core has no audio for a playing track, ao_read_data returns 0
and the worker wrote that: AudioTrack.write(..., 0) returns at once, so
the worker went round again with no wait - getPlayState, the latency
query, the read, ByteBuffer.clear and the write, a spin of JNI calls on
a full core for as long as the core had nothing. That is every file
whose audio ends before its video (the core leaves the AO streaming at
audio EOF and never stops it) and every underrun the core does not
pause the AO for. On a file with 8 s of audio and 40 s of video the
ao/audiotrack thread ran 87-91 % of a core after the audio ended: a
Pixel 7 drew 2.47 W instead of 0.47 W, a SEI box ran 2122 Mcycles/s
instead of 333.

The worker now waits on its condition instead, from KA_POLL_NS doubling
to KA_IDLE_NS while the core stays empty (18 wakeups/s at audio EOF), and
from the first wait again once audio flows. A seek, a resume or a
reopen goes through start(), which signals the worker at once; only an
underrun the core recovers from without one waits for the poll, against
a track that holds at least half a second. TrueHD groups that are
complete in the reassembly still go out. Steady playback, stream
silence and padded feeding are unchanged.

--- a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
@@ -246,6 +246,7 @@
                                    // the silence; stand the track down
     bool ka_stood_down;         // paused and empty until the core has audio
     int64_t ka_wait_ns;         // the next poll for audio while paused (KA_IDLE_NS)
+    int64_t idle_wait_ns;       // the next poll for the core's audio while it has none
     int64_t ka_feed_started_ns;
     unsigned ka_feed_units;
     uint32_t ka_head_seen;      // raw head at the last poll
@@ -3673,8 +3674,29 @@
                 // A PCM track stood down, and the core still has nothing:
                 // its padding is not written to the paused track.
                 AudioTrack_waitForAudio(ao);
+                continue;
+            } else if (!len && !write_pending(p) && !padded &&
+                       !(p->raw_passthrough && ao->format == AF_FORMAT_S_TRUEHD &&
+                         p->thd_complete >= THD_GROUP_UNITS)) {
+                // The core has no audio for the track (the audio ended before
+                // the video, or an underrun the core did not pause the AO
+                // for), and nothing is held for it. A zero-length write
+                // returns at once, so writing it would turn the worker into a
+                // spin of JNI calls for as long as the core has nothing. Wait
+                // instead, from KA_POLL_NS doubling up to KA_IDLE_NS while
+                // the core stays empty: a pull driver is not told when audio
+                // arrives (ao_start leaves a streaming driver alone), so the
+                // wait bounds how late audio after an underrun is written,
+                // against a track that holds at least half a second. A seek,
+                // a resume or a reopen calls start(), which signals the
+                // worker at once. TrueHD groups that are complete in the
+                // reassembly still go out (AudioTrack_thdGroup).
+                const int64_t wait = MPCLAMP(p->idle_wait_ns, KA_POLL_NS, KA_IDLE_NS);
+                mp_cond_timedwait(&p->wakeup, &p->lock, wait);
+                p->idle_wait_ns = MPMIN(wait * 2, KA_IDLE_NS);
                 continue;
             } else {
+                p->idle_wait_ns = 0;
                 if (padded) {
                     AudioTrack_keepAlivePad(ao);
                 } else if (p->ka_enabled || p->ka_pad_silence) {
